<title>GERMANY: Germans seek small free market barley export.</title>
<headline>Germans seek small free market barley export.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids for the export of 9,200 tonnes of free market barley, state grain intervention board BLE said.</p>
<p>They were seeking rebates in a 25.43 to 29.50 Ecus per tonne range, BLE added.</p>
<p>The export bids were made under the  weekly EU grain export tender.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
